   "definition_of_done": [
    "Output y is 1 for exactly five input codes: abcd = 0001 (1), 0111 (7), 1001 (9), 1011 (11), 1110 (14) with a as MSB; y is 0 for all other 11 combinations.",
    "Every gate has a unique identifier; no name is reused for both a gate instance and a signal wire (prevents L001 naming conflicts).",
    "Each gate uses exactly one of AND, OR, XOR, NOT; NOT gates have exactly 1 input; AND/OR/XOR have exactly 2 inputs; each gate drives exactly one output signal.",
    "Every gate output is connected to a defined destination (next gate, primary output, or left unconnected only if unused); no floating, dangling, or short-circuited outputs.",
    "Primary inputs a, b, c, d are correctly mapped with a as the most significant bit (MSB) of the 4-bit binary-encoded code.",
    "The sole output y is a single binary signal with no logical contradictions, hazards, or undefined states across all 16 input permutations.",
    "Only allowed gate types (AND, OR, XOR, NOT) are used throughout the design."
